WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
- You shared this season
that you're training yourself

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.130
to unlove your ex, Tristan.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.290
So, just how'd you do that?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.830
Asking for a friend.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.390
(group laughing)

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.500
Just I don't know,

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.102
if you have any paper or pen.

00:00:16.102 --> 00:00:16.935
(group laughing)

00:00:16.935 --> 00:00:17.768
No, it's hard.

00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:19.680
I think it's the most
ridiculous thing sometimes.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.700
When something doesn't work out

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.500
and you're in a relationship
and you're so deeply in love

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.510
and people are like, "oh,
yeah, well why can't you?"

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.000
And I'm like, I think I might
always still love that person.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.380
I don't know if that goes away.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.750
- No, and I don't think it
goes away like my ex-husband.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.390
I genuinely still love and
I want the best for him

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.320
and I'm rooting for him.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.153
- Absolutely.

00:00:35.153 --> 00:00:37.680
- We all, I think, just change or evolve,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.220
that sometimes it's just
not a right fit for you.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.390
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.210
- When I said I'm learning
how to unlove Tristan,

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.510
I think people, whether it be
family or friends or anyone

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.209
that you're telling your story to,

00:00:50.209 --> 00:00:52.230
they're like, "okay, so move on."

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.130
And I'm like, "No."

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.330
- Well, let me find the switch.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.163
- Right?

00:00:55.163 --> 00:00:56.460
It's not that easy.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.170
Just even the habits that you built,

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.880
the repetition, the routine.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.980
When something good happened,
I would call Tristan,

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.960
if something bad, that's what I did.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.900
Any little thing, I would
share my life with him,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.290
and so learning to just reprogram myself,

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.570
even though if someone
did something bad to me,

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.040
it doesn't just mean I'm like,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.630
there's a wall and I've built it up.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.660
I know that this isn't
the right thing for me

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.190
and I need to slowly heal and move on

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.873
but it doesn't happen over night.

